# -------------------------------------------------------
# node-bot environment variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values.
# Loaded automatically by the backend (node server.js) and the native
# launcher at startup; values here override the same variables inherited
# from your Windows environment.
# NEVER commit a .env file with real keys to Git.
# -------------------------------------------------------

# --- Keeping secrets out of this file (#645) ---
# Any value can point at where the secret lives instead of holding it:
#   MANA_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=keyring:Mana/discord
#     Windows Credential Manager (encrypted to your Windows account). Add it in
#     Control Panel > Credential Manager > Windows Credentials > "Add a generic
#     credential": address Mana/discord, any user name, the token as password.
#   MANA_DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=op://Private/Discord/token
#     1Password secret reference, read with the 1Password CLI (`op`) at startup.
# A reference that can't be read leaves the setting unset and logs why. Secrets
# (names ending in _TOKEN, _SECRET, _KEY, _PASSWORD) still written here in
# plain text work as before, but Doctor names them (a warning there only).

# --- AI replies ---
# Mana is local-first. OPENAI_API_KEY is ignored unless MANA_ALLOW_REMOTE_AI=1.
# Leave MANA_ALLOW_REMOTE_AI unset or set it to 0 for strictly local AI replies.
MANA_ALLOW_REMOTE_AI=0

# --- Network exposure (#670) ---
# The backend only accepts connections from this PC (127.0.0.1 and ::1).
# Anything that can reach it can make Mana reply and run tools, so leave this
# unset unless another device must connect directly (a launcher on another PC,
# curl from your phone on the same Wi-Fi). Then set 0.0.0.0 or this PC's LAN
# IP; Mana logs a warning and Doctor flags it. A Cloudflare tunnel does NOT
# need this: cloudflared connects to 127.0.0.1 itself.
# MANA_BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0

# --- Whisper (local STT) ---
WHISPER_BIN=C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\whisper\Release\whisper-cli.exe
# Unset: discovery picks the best model installed under tools\whisper, and a
# multilingual one when the speech language isn't English. Set it to pin one.
# WHISPER_MODEL=C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\whisper\models\ggml-large-v3-turbo-q5_0.bin
# Your own words for whisper to spell right, comma-separated, added to its
# prompt after your name. Keep it short (the prompt is capped) and drop a word
# if it starts turning up where you didn't say it.
WHISPER_VOCABULARY=Imouto, Oneesan, Gigi Murin, Hololive, VTuber

# --- Local llama ---
# Default here is the "default" profile (~8-15GB VRAM). Run `npm run doctor`
# for a hardware-based recommendation; on 15GB+ VRAM (e.g. RTX 5080) it'll
# suggest the "quality" profile instead -- point LLAMA_MODEL at that pick.
LLAMA_BIN=C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\llama\llama-b9436-bin-win-cuda-12.4-x64\llama-cli.exe
LLAMA_MODEL=C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\llama\gguf-models\Qwen3-4B-Q4_K_M.gguf
# Coding mode: C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\llama\gguf-models\qwen2.5-coder-7b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf
# Fast fallback: C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\llama\gguf-models\qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf
# Quality profile, 15GB+ VRAM: C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\llama\gguf-models\Qwen3-14B-Q4_K_M.gguf
# Quality fallback (if 14B unavailable): C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\llama\gguf-models\Qwen3-8B-Q4_K_M.gguf
# The model loads straight into VRAM by default (llama-server --load-mode
# none, not mmap'd into system RAM too: ~4GB less RAM for a 9B). Settings >
# Model toggles it; that saved choice wins over this env var, which turns
# mmap back on.
# MANA_LLAMA_MMAP=1
# llama-server's host-RAM prompt cache, in MiB (its own default is 8192 and
# it grows toward that). -1 = no limit, 0 = off.
# LLAMA_CACHE_RAM=1024
# CUDA unified memory for the chat llama-server (GGML_CUDA_ENABLE_UNIFIED_MEMORY).
# Off by default: on the RTX 5080 machine each server stop with it on left
# ~5 GB of RAM in use until a reboot. It made cold starts faster on an RTX
# 3070 Ti (docs/roadmap/issue-68-vram-hotswap-tuning.md). 1 = on.
# MANA_LLAMA_UNIFIED_MEMORY=1

# --- Sampler presets and thinking (#675) ---
# Sent with every local request (no llama-server restart), see
# ai/sampler-presets.js. Presets: stable (Qwen's non-thinking settings:
# temp 0.7, top_p 0.8, top_k 20, min_p 0), creative (+DRY/XTC), precise
# (temp 0.2), none (llama-server's own defaults). Defaults: coding=precise,
# every other profile=stable. Tool calls never get DRY/XTC.
# MANA_SAMPLER_PRESET=none
# MANA_SAMPLER_PRESET_DEFAULT=creative
# Tune or add presets without a code change in data/sampler-presets.json,
# e.g. {"creative": {"temperature": 0.9}, "mine": {"min_p": 0.05}} (merged
# over the built-in values, read on every request).
# Thinking is on for the quality and coding profiles, off for the rest, and
# always off for tool calls, streamed (spoken) replies, vision, Best-of-N and
# utility checks. Per profile or task (tools/stream/vision/bestofn/utility):
# MANA_THINKING_QUALITY=off
# MANA_THINKING_STREAM=on
# Thinking token budget, added on top of the reply's own max tokens (default 512):
# MANA_REASONING_BUDGET=512
# MANA_REASONING_BUDGET_CODING=1024
# Think harder: saying "think harder" / "think carefully" / "think it through",
# or the launcher's deep-thinking toggle, turns thinking on for that turn --
# tool calls and spoken replies included (Best-of-N is skipped) -- with its own
# budget (default 1024, ~11-13 s at 80-97 tokens/s; each tool-loop round at
# most 512), shrunk if the prompt would otherwise overflow the context. Mana
# can also turn it on herself when asked in other words, for up to 10 replies:
# MANA_THINK_HARDER_BUDGET=1024
# MANA_LLAMA_REASONING=on|off still switches thinking for everything at
# llama-server start and disables the per-request control above.

# --- Vision (screen/image description, optional) ---
# Auto-detected from a filename containing vl/vision/llava/minicpm-v/
# moondream/gemma-3/gemma-4 under tools\llama\gguf-models -- see
# docs\vision_setup.md. Some newer models (e.g. Qwen3.5) are natively
# multimodal and can serve as BOTH the default chat model and the vision
# model from the same weights, saving the model-swap cost between chat and
# vision use -- but their filename won't match the auto-detect regex, so
# point these at the same file as LLAMA_MODEL plus its mmproj explicitly.
# Use the Q8_0 mmproj: it reads images as well as F16 for ~280 MiB less
# VRAM (auto-detection also prefers *-Q8_0.gguf):
# LLAMA_VISION_MODEL=C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\llama\gguf-models\Qwen3.5-9B-Q4_K_M.gguf
# LLAMA_VISION_MMPROJ=C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\llama\gguf-models\mmproj-Qwen3.5-9B-Q8_0.gguf
# The chat server loads that mmproj on the first image (one reload) and
# drops it again after this long without an image (0 = keep it until the
# LLAMA_SERVER_IDLE_MS shutdown); a watched game starting drops it straight
# away.
# MANA_VISION_IDLE_MS=600000

# Gaming model: while a watched game (GAMING_PROCESS_NAMES) runs, the chat
# llama-server swaps to this smaller model, and back when the game ends.
# Unset = off (the normal model stays). The swap never lands mid-reply, the
# vision mmproj is never loaded with it (image turns go describe-first, or
# Mana says vision is paused while gaming), and Doctor and the tray status
# show "(gaming model)". Budget on a 16 GB RTX 5080: FFXIV + desktop ~5.1 GB
# and Fish on the GPU ~5.1 GB leave ~5.8 GB, too tight for the 9B at 16k.
# Default pick: Qwen3.5-4B IQ4_XS (2.5 GB file, unsloth/Qwen3.5-4B-GGUF).
# More headroom: Qwen3.5-2B Q8_0 (2.0 GB file, ~2.5 GB VRAM).
# For testing: the older Qwen3-1.7B-Q8_0.gguf.
# MANA_GAMING_LLAMA_MODEL=C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\llama\gguf-models\Qwen3.5-4B-IQ4_XS.gguf
# Its context (default 8192) and KV cache type (--cache-type-k/-v, default
# q8_0; a quantized V cache needs flash attention, which llama-server's
# default "auto" turns on, so don't set LLAMA_ARG_FLASH_ATTN=off with it).
# MANA_GAMING_LLAMA_CONTEXT=8192
# MANA_GAMING_KV_CACHE=q8_0
# Its host-RAM prompt cache in MiB (LLAMA_CACHE_RAM for the gaming model):
# system RAM, not VRAM, runs out first next to a game.
# MANA_GAMING_CACHE_RAM=256

# Held remarks wait while I play and may go out when I alt-tab away from
# the game. These apps in front still count as playing (a Discord call, OBS);
# the list replaces the default below.
# MANA_GAME_COMPANION_APPS=discord.exe,discordptb.exe,discordcanary.exe,obs64.exe,obs32.exe

# Standing reminders also fire on what's on screen (#1283), at most once per
# reminder per this many minutes. Windows of these apps, and InPrivate /
# Incognito / private-browsing windows, are never matched; the list replaces
# the default below.
# MANA_SCREEN_INTENT_COOLDOWN_MINUTES=30
# MANA_PRIVATE_APPS=keepass.exe,keepassxc.exe,1password.exe,bitwarden.exe,proton pass.exe

# --- Optional remote AI escape hatch ---
# Only set these if you intentionally want paid/proxy chat replies.
# MANA_ALLOW_REMOTE_AI=1
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-YOUR_KEY_HERE
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://new.aicode.us.com
# OPENAI_MODEL=codex-gpt-5.5

# --- TTS provider ---
# fish (S1-mini) is the default when unset. kokoro/gpt_sovits/qwen3tts are
# other choices -- set TTS_PROVIDER explicitly to use one of them instead. The
# native launcher starts only the selected one (no Fish Speech with gpt_sovits
# or qwen3tts).
# TTS_PROVIDER=fish
# Qwen3-TTS (TTS_PROVIDER=qwen3tts, setup in docs/qwen3_tts.md). The service
# listens on 127.0.0.1 at QWEN3_TTS_URL's port and clones the FISH_TTS_REF_*
# clip unless QWEN3_TTS_REF_* are set. It stays loaded while gaming. No
# fallback by default: a reply it can't voice shows as text (=kokoro speaks it
# through Kokoro instead). Values below are the defaults.
# QWEN3_TTS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5012
# QWEN3_TTS_MODEL_DIR=C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\qwen3-tts\models\Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-Base
# QWEN3_TTS_REF_AUDIO=
# QWEN3_TTS_REF_TEXT=
# QWEN3_TTS_FALLBACK_PROVIDER=none
# Kokoro (Fish's voice while gaming) is started on demand and stopped after this
# long unused (default 600000 = 10 min; 0 keeps it running once started).
# MANA_KOKORO_IDLE_MS=600000

# The Python retriever (tools/retriever_service.py, coding-mode repo search
# fallback after tools/retriever-index; needs a built tools/vector_store with
# index.ann + metadata.sqlite, ~0.5 GB RAM settled, #809) is started by the
# first coding turn that needs it and stopped after this long unused (default
# 600000 = 10 min; 2 min while gaming, and at once when a watched game
# starts). A store that only has the old metadata.json needs
# `python tools/metadata_db.py tools/vector_store` or a rebuild with
# tools/ingest_codebase.py. MANA_START_RETRIEVER=1 makes the native launcher
# start it at launch instead; one started that way is never stopped.
# MANA_RETRIEVER_IDLE_MS=600000
# MANA_START_RETRIEVER=1

# --- Mobile PWA companion ---
# Generate MOBILE_PASSCODE_HASH from node-bot without putting the passcode in shell history:
# $p = Read-Host -AsSecureString "Mana mobile passcode"; $b = [Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::SecureStringToBSTR($p); try { [Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::PtrToStringBSTR($b) | node -e "const fs = require('fs'); const { hashPasscode } = require('./mobile-auth'); const pass = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf8').replace(/\r?\n$/, ''); console.log(hashPasscode(pass));" } finally { [Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::ZeroFreeBSTR($b) }
MOBILE_PASSCODE_HASH=pbkdf2_sha256$120000$REPLACE_SALT$REPLACE_HASH

# Generate with:
# node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
MOBILE_SESSION_SECRET=replace-with-random-hex
MOBILE_SESSION_TTL_MS=43200000
MOBILE_MEMORY_DIR=C:\ManaAI\Mana\node-bot\data

# --- Browser request guard (#670) ---
# Requests whose Host header is a hostname other than "localhost" (IP
# addresses are fine) are refused, which blocks DNS-rebinding pages. Reaching Mana
# through a tunnel or DNS name? List it here (MANA_TUNNEL_URL's host is
# allowed automatically). Comma-separated.
# MANA_ALLOWED_HOSTS=mana.example.com
# Browser pages may only POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE (or open a WebSocket) from
# Mana's own pages, the Electron launchers (file://) and browser extensions.
# Add another exact origin of your own here. Comma-separated.
# MANA_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
# Admin actions (restart, account and mobile-device management, llama.cpp
# updates, skill import) no longer trust a request just for coming from this
# PC. The native launcher sends its own per-run key; scripts, curl and the
# /admin pages send this as the x-admin-token header. Generate with:
# node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# ADMIN_TOKEN=

# --- Local-only mode (#670) ---
# 1 = nothing leaves this PC and your local network. Cloud AI can't be set
# up, and anything that would connect elsewhere (web search, page reading,
# Wikipedia, video downloads, browser automation, plugin installs, the
# Discord/Telegram/Matrix bridges, a cloud TTS) fails with an explanation.
# LAN machines count as local when given by IP address. MCP servers that
# run as their own program (stdio) aren't started. Off by default; the
# native launcher's Settings > Connection toggle turns it on too.
# MANA_LOCAL_ONLY=1

# --- Tool approval (#669) ---
# Which tool calls wait for your OK: smart (default) = anything that isn't
# read-only, ask = every call, off = only destructive ones (destructive calls
# always ask). Settings > Approvals sets it; that saved choice wins over this.
# MANA_TOOL_APPROVAL=smart

# --- Image generation (plugins/image-generation, off by default in Settings > Plugins) ---
# Local-first: point at your own already-running instance.
# MANA_IMAGE_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:7860
# MANA_IMAGE_BACKEND_TYPE=automatic1111 is the default when MANA_IMAGE_BACKEND_URL
# is set (Automatic1111 WebUI's /sdapi/v1/txt2img). Set to "comfyui" to talk to a
# ComfyUI instance at the same URL instead (issue #225 -- legacy single-checkpoint
# workflow only; split-loader models like FLUX/Mage-Flow need issue #271, not yet
# implemented).
# MANA_IMAGE_BACKEND_TYPE=comfyui
# Required when MANA_IMAGE_BACKEND_TYPE=comfyui -- ComfyUI's workflow graph always
# names an exact checkpoint file (unlike Automatic1111, which just uses whatever's
# already loaded). Must match a file in your ComfyUI install's models/checkpoints/.
# MANA_IMAGE_COMFYUI_CHECKPOINT=sd_xl_base_1.0.safetensors
# Optional -- how long to poll /history before giving up on a generation (default 120000).
# MANA_IMAGE_COMFYUI_TIMEOUT_MS=120000
# External API, opt-in only (never a default) -- used only if MANA_IMAGE_BACKEND_URL is unset.
# MANA_IMAGE_API_KEY=sk-YOUR_KEY_HERE
# MANA_IMAGE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# --- Memory recall (issue #674) ---
# Remembered facts injected per reply: up to 5 pinned (Settings > Memory Facts)
# plus this many matched by key, keyword or embedding similarity (default 5).
# MANA_MEMORY_MAX_MATCHED_FACTS=5
# How long to wait for the embedder to embed the message before recall falls
# back to key/keyword matching only (default 1000 ms).
# MANA_MEMORY_RECALL_TIMEOUT_MS=1000
# Optional CPU-only reranker: orders recall candidates when more match than
# fit, and trims session_search results to the best 8. Off unless this names
# a local .gguf file -- nothing is downloaded automatically. Recommended:
# bge-reranker-v2-m3 Q8_0 (636 MB), from
# https://huggingface.co/gpustack/bge-reranker-v2-m3-GGUF
# Runs a second llama-server with -ngl 0 and the GPU hidden (no VRAM), started
# at backend startup (skipped while a watched game runs) and at the start of each
# user turn, and stopped after MANA_RERANKER_IDLE_MS (default 3600000, 1 hour).
# MANA_RERANKER_MODEL=C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\llama\gguf-models\bge-reranker-v2-m3-Q8_0.gguf
# MANA_RERANKER_PORT=8091
# Per-call budget; on timeout the candidates keep their unreranked order.
# MANA_RERANKER_TIMEOUT_MS=1500
# How many best-first candidates are scored per call (the rest keep their order);
# ~0.5 s warm on CPU for 10 vs ~1.1 s for 20.
# MANA_RERANKER_MAX_CANDIDATES=10
# Optional GPU embedder for semantic memory search, replacing the Python
# tools/local_embedder.py service (RETRIEVER_EMBEDDER_URL). Off unless this
# names a local .gguf file -- nothing is downloaded automatically.
# Recommended: Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B Q8_0 (639 MB), from
# https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B-GGUF (the model the Python
# service runs). Runs a llama-server with --embedding fully on the GPU
# (~2.3 GB VRAM, ~0.5 GB RAM), started at backend startup (skipped while a
# watched game runs) and at the start of each user turn, and stopped after
# MANA_EMBEDDER_IDLE_MS (default 3600000, 1 hour); when set, the native
# launcher no longer starts the Python service. Texts over 2048 characters are
# embedded in overlapping chunks and averaged.
# MANA_EMBEDDER_MODEL=C:\ManaAI\Mana\tools\llama\gguf-models\Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B-Q8_0.gguf
# MANA_EMBEDDER_PORT=8092

# --- Memory vault (issue #935) ---
# Two-way sync between Mana's remembered facts and an Obsidian vault: one
# note per fact in <vault>\Facts, kept up to date automatically. Editing a
# note updates the fact; a new note waits for your OK in Mana; deleting one
# archives the fact. Off unless set.
# MANA_VAULT_DIR=D:\ManaAI\Mana-Obsidian\Mana

# --- Crisis support (issue #1040) ---
# A message about suicide or self-harm gets a care note with these contacts
# for that reply. Defaults to the Singapore lines below; set your own here.
# MANA_CRISIS_HOTLINES=Samaritans of Singapore (SOS) 24-hour hotline: 1767; IMH Mental Health Helpline: 6389 2222

# --- Self-work: Gemini CLI fallback (issue #1269) ---
# When every local attempt at one of my issues fails, Mana can ask Gemini
# CLI (signed in with your own Google account) to try, then checks, tests
# and reviews its change like her own before any PR. Install it with
#   npm install -g @google/gemini-cli
# and run gemini once to choose Sign in with Google. On by default once it is
# installed and signed in; off in local-only mode. Its tools are limited to
# reading, searching and editing files in her worktree.
# MANA_SELF_WORK_GEMINI=0
# MANA_SELF_WORK_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash   (unset: the CLI's default)
# MANA_SELF_WORK_GEMINI_PER_ISSUE=1
# MANA_SELF_WORK_GEMINI_PER_DAY=5

# --- Self-work: training traces (issue #1287) ---
# Her PRs whose tests and review passed are kept (scrubbed) in
# data/self-work-traces/ for a later fine-tune of her local model; Gemini
# CLI's changes never are. See docs/self_work_training_traces.md.
# MANA_SELF_WORK_TRACES=0
# MANA_SELF_WORK_TRACES_MAX_MB=200
